$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The graph of the function <span class="italic">f</span>, defined by <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_001_3a50a4d0.png" alt="f of x equals, negative one-half times, open parenthesis, x minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10"></span></span>, is shown in the <span class="italic"><span class="italic ">xy</span></span>-plane above. If the function <span class="italic">g</span> (not shown) is defined by <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_002_a0c4d76a.png" alt="g of x equals, negative x plus 10"></span></span>, what is one possible value of <span class="italic">a</span> such that <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_003_8c6e1419.png" alt="f of a equals, g of a"></span></span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["either 2","8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is either 2 or 8. Substituting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_004_edc21642.png" alt="x equals a"></span> in the definitions for <span class="italic">f</span> and <span class="italic">g</span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_005_ce44c330.png" alt="f of a, equals, negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_006_9b5429c7.png" alt="g of a, equals, negative a, plus 10"></span>, respectively. If <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_007_8c6e1419.png" alt="f of a, equals, g of a"></span>, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_008_c593f401.png" alt="negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10, equals, negative a, plus 10"></span>. Subtracting 10 from both sides of this equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_009_b6c4d5e2.png" alt="negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals negative a"></span>. Multiplying both sides by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_010_ebe7b417.png" alt="negative 2"></span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_011_7c0dde7b.png" alt="open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals 2 a"></span>. Expanding <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_012_a2e86c3f.png" alt="open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_013_338f4f74.png" alt="a, squared, minus 8 a, plus 16, equals 2 a"></span>. Combining the like terms on one side of the equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_014_2fe92f92.png" alt="a, squared, minus 10 a, plus 16, equals 0"></span>. One way to solve this equation is to factor <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_015_29c75e5f.png" alt="a, squared, minus 10 a, plus 16"></span> by identifying two numbers with a sum of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_016_fdf646a6.png" alt="negative 10"></span> and a product of 16. These numbers are <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_017_ebe7b417.png" alt="negative 2"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_018_db570df6.png" alt="negative 8"></span>, so the quadratic equation can be factored as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_019_2b562421.png" alt="open parenthesis, a, minus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, a, minus 8, close parenthesis, equals 0"></span>. Therefore, the possible values of <span class="italic">a</span> are either 2 or 8. Note that 2 and 8 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.<p>Alternate approach: Graphically, the condition <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_020_8c6e1419.png" alt="f of a, equals, g of a"></span> implies the graphs of the functions <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_021_448547e8.png" alt="y equals f of x"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_022_fabe5a3e.png" alt="y equals g of x"></span> intersect at <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_023_edc21642.png" alt="x equals a"></span>. The graph <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_024_448547e8.png" alt="y equals f of x"></span> is given, and the graph of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_025_fabe5a3e.png" alt="y equals g of x"></span> may be sketched as a line with <span class="italic">y</span>-intercept 10 and a slope of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_026_d3b569af.png" alt="negative 1"></span> (taking care to note the different scales on each axis). These two graphs intersect at <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_027_4a24f52d.png" alt="x equals 2"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_028_1d4468f6.png" alt="x equals 8"></span>.</p></p>
$SATQ$, true, 29, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"97e50fa2","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"070621-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_000_7824a464.png\" alt=\"The figure presents the graph of a curve in the xy-plane. The curve is labeled y equals f of x. The numbers 0 through 9 are indicated on the x-axis. The numbers 0 through 12, in increments of 2, are indicated on the y-axis. The curve begins at the point with coordinates 0 comma 2 and moves upward and to the right reaching a maximum at the point with coordinates 4 comma 10. It turns and moves downward and to the right, ending at 8 point 5 on the x-axis\" width=\"222\" height=\"169\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The graph of the function <span class=\"italic\">f</span>, defined by <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_001_3a50a4d0.png\" alt=\"f of x equals, negative one-half times, open parenthesis, x minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10\"></span></span>, is shown in the <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">xy</span></span>-plane above. If the function <span class=\"italic\">g</span> (not shown) is defined by <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_002_a0c4d76a.png\" alt=\"g of x equals, negative x plus 10\"></span></span>, what is one possible value of <span class=\"italic\">a</span> such that <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_003_8c6e1419.png\" alt=\"f of a equals, g of a\"></span></span> ?</p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["either 2","8"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is either 2 or 8. Substituting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_004_edc21642.png\" alt=\"x equals a\"></span> in the definitions for <span class=\"italic\">f</span> and <span class=\"italic\">g</span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_005_ce44c330.png\" alt=\"f of a, equals, negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_006_9b5429c7.png\" alt=\"g of a, equals, negative a, plus 10\"></span>, respectively. If <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_007_8c6e1419.png\" alt=\"f of a, equals, g of a\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_008_c593f401.png\" alt=\"negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10, equals, negative a, plus 10\"></span>. Subtracting 10 from both sides of this equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_009_b6c4d5e2.png\" alt=\"negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals negative a\"></span>. Multiplying both sides by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_010_ebe7b417.png\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_011_7c0dde7b.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals 2 a\"></span>. Expanding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_012_a2e86c3f.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared\"></span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_013_338f4f74.png\" alt=\"a, squared, minus 8 a, plus 16, equals 2 a\"></span>. Combining the like terms on one side of the equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_014_2fe92f92.png\" alt=\"a, squared, minus 10 a, plus 16, equals 0\"></span>. One way to solve this equation is to factor <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_015_29c75e5f.png\" alt=\"a, squared, minus 10 a, plus 16\"></span> by identifying two numbers with a sum of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_016_fdf646a6.png\" alt=\"negative 10\"></span> and a product of 16. These numbers are <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_017_ebe7b417.png\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_018_db570df6.png\" alt=\"negative 8\"></span>, so the quadratic equation can be factored as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_019_2b562421.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, a, minus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, a, minus 8, close parenthesis, equals 0\"></span>. Therefore, the possible values of <span class=\"italic\">a</span> are either 2 or 8. Note that 2 and 8 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.<p>Alternate approach: Graphically, the condition <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_020_8c6e1419.png\" alt=\"f of a, equals, g of a\"></span> implies the graphs of the functions <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_021_448547e8.png\" alt=\"y equals f of x\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_022_fabe5a3e.png\" alt=\"y equals g of x\"></span> intersect at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_023_edc21642.png\" alt=\"x equals a\"></span>. The graph <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_024_448547e8.png\" alt=\"y equals f of x\"></span> is given, and the graph of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_025_fabe5a3e.png\" alt=\"y equals g of x\"></span> may be sketched as a line with <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept 10 and a slope of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_026_d3b569af.png\" alt=\"negative 1\"></span> (taking care to note the different scales on each axis). These two graphs intersect at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_027_4a24f52d.png\" alt=\"x equals 2\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/97e50fa2/img_028_1d4468f6.png\" alt=\"x equals 8\"></span>.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":29,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959631,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"97e50fa2","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959631,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"070621-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"5361a02e-9b23-4251-93b8-5cc489b48d48","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"070621-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents the graph of a curve in the xy-plane. The curve is labeled y equals f of x. The numbers 0 through 9 are indicated on the x-axis. The numbers 0 through 12, in increments of 2, are indicated on the y-axis. The curve begins at the point with coordinates 0 comma 2 and moves upward and to the right reaching a maximum at the point with coordinates 4 comma 10. It turns and moves downward and to the right, ending at 8 point 5 on the x-axis\" width=\"222\" height=\"169\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The graph of the function <span class=\"italic\">f</span>, defined by <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of x equals, negative one-half times, open parenthesis, x minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10\"></span></span>, is shown in the <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">xy</span></span>-plane above. If the function <span class=\"italic\">g</span> (not shown) is defined by <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"g of x equals, negative x plus 10\"></span></span>, what is one possible value of <span class=\"italic\">a</span> such that <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of a equals, g of a\"></span></span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is either 2 or 8. Substituting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals a\"></span> in the definitions for <span class=\"italic\">f</span> and <span class=\"italic\">g</span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of a, equals, negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"g of a, equals, negative a, plus 10\"></span>, respectively. If <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of a, equals, g of a\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 10, equals, negative a, plus 10\"></span>. Subtracting 10 from both sides of this equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative one half times, open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals negative a\"></span>. Multiplying both sides by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals 2 a\"></span>. Expanding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, a, minus 4, close parenthesis, squared\"></span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, squared, minus 8 a, plus 16, equals 2 a\"></span>. Combining the like terms on one side of the equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, squared, minus 10 a, plus 16, equals 0\"></span>. One way to solve this equation is to factor <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, squared, minus 10 a, plus 16\"></span> by identifying two numbers with a sum of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 10\"></span> and a product of 16. These numbers are <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 8\"></span>, so the quadratic equation can be factored as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, a, minus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, a, minus 8, close parenthesis, equals 0\"></span>. Therefore, the possible values of <span class=\"italic\">a</span> are either 2 or 8. Note that 2 and 8 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.<p>Alternate approach: Graphically, the condition <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of a, equals, g of a\"></span> implies the graphs of the functions <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals f of x\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals g of x\"></span> intersect at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals a\"></span>. The graph <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals f of x\"></span> is given, and the graph of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals g of x\"></span> may be sketched as a line with <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept 10 and a slope of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABcAAAAYCAYAAAARfGZ1AAAACXBIWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAABGJhU0UAAAAMyZLetQAAAFhJREFUeNpjYKAMtADxNiB+DsT/oXyqgS9AfAyIp9LCcCYkNtUNZyDWcBEiMBu5hv8nAoeQa7gLEViMXMNpGuYjy/AQJAwyfA0SnyquxYVHwSgYBaOAJgAAQ7AqWC3zu8cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=\" alt=\"negative 1\"></span> (taking care to note the different scales on each axis). These two graphs intersect at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 2\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 8\"></span>.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959631,"updateDate":1691007959631,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959631, 1691007959631)