Choice D is correct. Adding <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the given equation yields <math alttext=\"w squared plus 12 w equals 40\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>40</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. To complete the square, adding <math alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction 12 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"6 squared\"><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, to both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"w squared plus 12 w plus 6 squared equals 40 plus 6 squared\"><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"left parenthesis w plus 6 right parenthesis squared equals 76\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>76</mn></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"w plus 6 equals plus or minus StartRoot 76 EndRoot\"><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>76</mn></msqrt></math>, or <math alttext=\"w plus 6 equals plus or minus 2 StartRoot 19 EndRoot\"><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>19</mn></msqrt></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"w equals negative 6 plus or minus 2 StartRoot 19 EndRoot\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>19</mn></msqrt></math>. Therefore, the solutions to the given equation are <math alttext=\"negative 6 plus 2 StartRoot 19 EndRoot\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>19</mn></msqrt></math>